// Title: Explorer NOUACCHECK Flag
// Sigma ID: 534f2ef7-e8a2-4433-816d-c91bccde289b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-23 | Modified: 2022-04-21
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects suspicious starts of explorer.exe that use the /NOUACCHECK flag that allows to run all
//   sub processes of that newly started explorer.exe without any UAC checks
// False positives:
//   - Domain Controller User Logon
//   - Unknown how many legitimate software products use that method
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/ORCA6665/status/1496478087244095491
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_explorer_nouaccheck.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/NOUACCHECK") and (not((InitiatingProcessCommandLine =~ "C:\\Windows\\system32\\svchost.exe -k netsvcs -p -s Schedule" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe")))
